# DO NOT

- Do not state versions, library APIs, config filenames, or release history
  from memory. Verify with a command (`cat package.json`, `npx <pkg> --version`,
  `npm ls <pkg>`) or say "I can't verify this" and stop.
- Do not use JavaScript animation libraries (GSAP, Framer Motion, AOS).
- Do not create files that were not requested, or add sections beyond the ask.
- Do not continue past 5 tool calls without stopping for review.

# This project's stack (verified — do not assume otherwise)

- Astro 7.x. Tailwind 4.x, CSS-first: there is NO tailwind.config.mjs and you
  must not create one. Theme tokens go in src/styles/global.css under @theme.
- Scaffold and add integrations with official tooling, always with --yes
  (`npx astro add <name> --yes`). Interactive prompts hang the terminal.

# Build standards

- Target 100 Lighthouse across all four categories.
- Zero client-side JS by default. Any JS needs a stated reason.
- Use Astro's <Image /> component, never raw <img>.
- Wrap all animation in a prefers-reduced-motion guard.
- Scroll animations use animation-timeline: view(), not load-triggered keyframes.

# Scope

- One component per task. Stop when it's done and wait.
- When asked to change a file, change only that file. Name any other file you
  believe needs changing and wait for approval.
# SEO

- Read SEO-PLAN.md before building any page or component. Its §8 checklist is
  part of "done" for every task.
